1. Definitions

1.1 “Materials” means the AetherCell repository, code, model weights,
checkpoints, tokenizer or vocabulary files if any, prompts, templates,
configurations, documentation, metadata, evaluation assets, and associated
files made available by the licensors.

1.2 “Output” means any result, prediction, score, ranking, embedding,
generated content, analysis result, hypothesis, or other output produced
in whole or in part using the Materials.

1.3 “Derivative Material” means any modified, adapted, fine-tuned,
continued-trained, distilled, merged, extended, improved, translated,
ported, wrapped, reparameterized, compressed, quantized, or otherwise
derived version of the Materials, in whole or in part.

1.4 “Public Disclosure” means any public or semi-public communication,
including but not limited to a manuscript, preprint, journal article,
conference paper, poster, thesis, benchmark report, technical report,
presentation, model card, dataset card, web page, repository page,
Hugging Face page, API documentation, press release, blog post, or other
public-facing document or release.

1.5 “Non-Commercial Research Use” means use solely for academic,
scholarly, educational, or internal scientific research purposes, and
not for commercial advantage, monetary compensation, fee-for-service,
productization, clinical deployment, or other commercial exploitation.

